# {{PROJECT_NAME}} — a 1C-Bitrix (on-premise) project

## Project Map

- `/local/` — all custom code: components, templates, modules
- `/local/php_interface/` — init scripts and event handlers
- `/local/components/` — custom components (complex preferred)
- `/local/templates/.default/` — site template
- `/local/modules/` — custom modules (reusable functionality)
- `/bitrix/` — core and standard modules (MUST NOT modify)

## Vendor Convention

- Vendor name MUST be: `{{VENDOR_NAME}}` (confirmed at initialization)
- Top-level namespace MUST be: `{{VENDOR_NAME}}\`
- Module prefix MUST be: `{{vendor_name}}.<modulename>` (e.g. `{{vendor_name}}.billing`)
- Custom components and JS MUST live in: `local/components/{{vendor_name}}/`, `local/js/{{vendor_name}}/`
- CSS prefixes MUST be: `{{vendor_name}}-`
- DB table prefix MUST be: `{{db_prefix}}` (derived from vendor name, e.g. `acme` for `Acme`; max 5 chars) — used as `{{db_prefix}}_table_name`

## Ground Rules

| Rule | Use When |
| --- | --- |
| `@.agents/rules/core/core-interaction.md` | Any work touching `init.php`, event handlers, agents (scheduled tasks), components, form handling/CSRF, or logging |
| `@.agents/rules/core/database.md` | Any work with D7 ORM entities, direct SQL (rare, ORM-first), migrations, or DB table naming (`{{db_prefix}}`) |
| `@.agents/rules/core/architecture.md` | Creating or moving files: modules, components, classes, namespaces (PSR-4) |
| `@.agents/rules/core/code-style.md` | Writing or editing any PHP code: naming, formatting (PSR-12 + Bitrix deviations), strict typing, PHPDoc |
| `@.agents/rules/core/gitflow.md` | Any git work: branches (Git Flow), commits (Conventional Commits), PRs, releases |

## Working Principles

- Plan before non-trivial changes
- Clarify ambiguous requirements instead of guessing
- Test changes in staging before rollout
- Fail fast with explicit error messages
- Keep the change scope small — one task at a time

## Commands

All commands run from `/local/` (the composer root).

```bash
cd local

# Syntax check for a single file
php -l <file>

# Single-file style check
php vendor/bin/phpcs --standard=.phpcs.xml --extensions=php <path>
php vendor/bin/php-cs-fixer fix --dry-run --diff --config=.php-cs-fixer.dist.php -- <path>
```

